_on":"2025-09-15T00:00:00Z","closed_at":"2025-09-18T17:13:14Z"},"comments":2,"created_at":"2025-07-10T18:47:19Z","updated_at":"2025-07-15T13:10:26Z","closed_at":"2025-07-15T13:10:24Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nInitially discovered on 4.5.beta1. Persists up to, and including, beta3.\n\nDoes **not** occur on 4.4.1 or 4.4.\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.beta1 - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Mobile) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7652) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-9900K CPU @ 3.60GHz (16 threads) - 31.92 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe red/white resize gizmo for SphereShape3D-s does not update whenever the shape is part of a CollisionShape3D. The gizmo itself is still fully operational, it is simply frozen in a default position.\n\nInterestingly, this bug does **not** happen when creating and modifying a CSGSphere3D, although it ostensibly features the exact same gizmo.\n\nHere are some quick screenshots:\n\n<img width=\"659\" height=\"605\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c87c4069-a829-4238-a539-0209290e5408\" />\n\n<img width=\"455\" height=\"327\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1b22a8e6-f4c2-45f1-bf47-74568530b29d\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create/open a 3D scene.\n2. Add a CollisionShape3D node and provide it with a new SphereShape3D.\n3. Play around with the sphere's size, either by clicking and dragging the gizmo or through the inspector.\n4. Observe that the resize gizmo does not follow the sphere's actual size.\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":